1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 d6 5. c3 Nf6 6. d4 Bd7 7. O-O Be7 8. Re1
O-O 9. Nbd2 Re8 10. Bb3 ({Another plan is} 10. a3 Bf8 11. b4 {with the
possible sequel} d5 12. Bb3 Bg4 13. exd5 Nxd5 14. Bb2 Qd7 15. Bxd5 Qxd5 16. c4
Bxf3 17. cxd5 Bxd1 18. dxc6 Ba4 19. cxb7 Rab8 20. dxe5 {and White has won a
pawn.}) 10... h6 11. Nf1 Bf8 12. Ng3 Bg4 $146 13. h3 Bxf3 14. Qxf3 {Pawns
don't matter to Littlewood!} exd4 15. Nf5 $17 (15. Nh5 $5 {looks like a viable
alternative} dxc3 16. bxc3 $15) 15... d5 (15... dxc3 16. Qg3 {is strong for
White.}) 16. Bxh6 {He's not petty with his pieces either!} Nxe4 {Gligoric
takes no chances and by declining White's sacrifice secures rather the better
ending. 16...gxh6 is not clear but White certainly has good attacking
prospects.} 17. Bf4 Ne5 $11 (17... dxc3 $5 {has some apparent merit} 18. bxc3
Bc5 $17 (18... Bc5 19. Ne3 Ne5 20. Bxe5 $15)) (17... g5 18. h4 (18. Bh2 dxc3
$15)) 18. Bxe5 Rxe5 19. Rad1 $11 (19. Qf4 Re8 20. Qg4 c6 $14 (20... dxc3 $2 {
doesn't work because of} 21. Nh6+ Kh7 22. Nxf7 $18)) 19... Qd7 20. Nxd4 Rae8 (
20... c5 21. Qf4 $11 (21. Nc2 Rae8 22. Qf4 Qd8 $11)) 21. Qg4 $17 ({Probably
the last move White wanted to make. Black had threatened to win at once with
21...Nd2.} 21. Qd3 $142 $5 {must definitely be considered} Nc5 22. Qd2 Nxb3 23.
Nxb3 Rxe1+ 24. Rxe1 Rxe1+ 25. Qxe1 $15) (21. Qf4 Bd6 22. Nf3 R5e7 23. Qh4 $15)
(21. Qe3 Bc5 22. a4 $11) 21... Qxg4 $15 (21... Nf6 22. Rxe5 Nxg4 23. Rxd5 $17)
22. hxg4 c6 23. f3 Nc5 24. Rxe5 Rxe5 25. Bc2 g6 26. Kf2 Bg7 27. a4 Re7 28. a5
Be5 29. b4 Nd7 (29... Bxd4+ 30. cxd4 $14 (30. Rxd4 Nd7 31. Rd1 Kh7 $14)) 30.
Bb3 Nf8 31. Rd3 Kg7 32. Ne2 Ne6 33. c4 (33. Rd1 Kf6 $11) 33... dxc4 34. Bxc4
Nc7 $2 {Short of time, Gligoric doesn't realise that his bishop is in danger.}
35. f4 Bb2 $11 ({If} 35... Bf6 36. g5) 36. Rb3 Re4 $2 $16 ({Losing quickly.} 
36... Ba1 {was correct} 37. Rb1 Re4 38. Bd3 Bd4+ 39. Kf1 Re3 {etc.}) 37. Bd3 $1
{retaining the advantage} ({Instead of} 37. Rxb2 Rxc4 38. g5 Nd5 $15) 37...
Bd4+ 38. Kf1 ({Less advisable is} 38. Nxd4 Rxd4 39. Ke3 Rxb4 40. Rxb4 Nd5+ 41.
Ke4 Nxb4 $15) (38. Kf3 $4 Re3+ 39. Kf2 Rxd3+) 38... Re3 $2 (38... Rxe2 $142 39.
Bxe2 Nd5 $18) 39. Nxd4 Nd5 40. Kf2 Re7 {With characteristic calmness,
Littlewood, though he had plenty of time, carried on playing at full speed. No
scurrying for the adjournment.} 41. g3 Rd7 42. Nc2 Nf6 43. Kf3 Rd5 44. g5 Ne8
45. Ne3 Rd4 46. f5 Nd6 47. Bc2 Ne8 48. f6+ {Source: John Littlewood collection
(Keith Brown)} 1-0

