1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Be2 O-O 6. O-O Nbd7 7. e5 ({Some
sources for this game have} 7. Re1 c5 8. e5 Ne8 {here, but the text move order
is given in CHESS.}) 7... Ne8 8. Re1 c5 9. e6 $15 ({This turns out badly for
White.} 9. Bf4 $142 $16) 9... fxe6 {Robatsch's central pawn mass now turns out
to be too powerful.} 10. Ng5 $17 (10. Be3 $5 $15) 10... Nc7 $15 (10... Bxd4 11.
Nxe6 Bxf2+ 12. Kh1 $16) 11. Be3 cxd4 12. Bxd4 e5 $14 (12... Nf6 $142 $5 $15 {
would keep Black alive}) 13. Be3 $15 (13. Bc4+ $142 $5 {is noteworthy} Kh8 14.
Be3 $14) 13... Nf6 14. Bc4+ $17 (14. f4 $5 exf4 15. Bxf4 $15) 14... d5 15. Bb3
Qd6 16. Qd2 Kh8 $15 (16... e6 $5 $17) 17. f4 (17. Rad1 Bf5 $15) 17... Ng4 $11 (
17... e4 $5 {must be considered} 18. Bd4 h6 $17) 18. Nxd5 Nxe3 19. Rxe3 $4 $19
{there were better ways to keep up the pressure} (19. Ne4 Qd8 20. Nxc7 Qxc7 21.
Qxe3 exf4 22. Qc1 $19) 19... exf4 20. Rxe7 {Black gets strong play along the
open e-file} Nxd5 $1 {surprise!} 21. Rxg7 (21. Nf7+ Rxf7 22. Rxf7 Bxb2 $19)
21... Kxg7 22. Bxd5 (22. Qxd5 Qxd5 23. Bxd5 Rf5 24. Ne6+ Bxe6 25. Bxe6 Re5 $19)
22... Qc5+ (22... Qb6+ $142 {might be the shorter path} 23. Kh1 Qxb2 $19) 23.
Kh1 Rf5 (23... Bg4 24. Ne4 Qc7 25. Qb4 $19) 24. Ne6+ (24. Bxb7 Rb8 25. Ne4 Qa5
26. Bxc8 Qxd2 27. Nxd2 Rd5 $19) 24... Bxe6 25. Bxe6 Re5 26. Bg4 (26. Qd7+ Kh6
27. Rf1 Rf8 $19) 26... Rae8 27. h3 (27. Rf1 g5 $19) 27... Qe3 28. Rd1 Qg3 29.
Qc3 (29. Qd4 {otherwise it's curtains at once} Kh6 30. Rg1 $19) 29... Qxc3 30.
bxc3 Re1+ $1 {a check from hell} 31. Kh2 Rxd1 32. Bxd1 Re3 {Sources: CHESS/27/
401-2, January 1962, p39; John Littlewood collection (Keith Brown)} (32... Re3
33. c4 Rc3 $19) 0-1

