Bf4 Bxc5 9. Qg4 g5 10. Qxg5 Qxg5 11. Bxg5 Nxe5 12. Bf6 Bxf2+ 13. Ke2 Nxc4 14.
Bxh8 Bxg1 $6 15. Rhxg1 Nxb2 16. g4 b6 17. Rg3 Ke7 18. c4 Nxc4 19. Rh3 Ba6 $2
20. Rxh7 Rg8 21. Kf3 Bb7+ 22. Kf4 e5+ 23. Kg3 Be4 24. Rh6 f5 25. Bf6+ Kf7 26.
g5 f4+ 27. Kf2 Bd3 28. h4 e4 29. Bc3 Ne3 30. Rg1 Nd5 31. Bb2 c5 $2 32. h5 c4
33. Bd4 c3 34. Rd6 Bc4 35. h6 c2 36. h7 Rxg5 37. h8=Q Rxg1 38. Rxd7+ Ke6 39.
Qe8+ Kf5 40. Qf8+ Ke6 41. Qf7# {"Last few moves unclear due to squiggles on
score sheet in Zeitnot. Game ended by 41 Qf7# with Wh R on [e8]? Bl K on e6. I
have never been able to reconstruct satisfactorily. Maybe I recorded 38 Qh7+
when 38 Rxd7+ was actually played? I should have at least drawn earlier. It
still rankles decades later! The Pole Mannke was soon to die in a car accident
back home and could not take up his Premier place." " (Source: Bernard
Cafferty)} 1-0

